  "metadata": {
    "note": "opencode as an AI agent: `mcp_servers` (agent opencode, written straight into ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json) and `ai_skills` method opencode-plugin (`opencode plugin add/remove` through su). For the QEMU VM harness (scripts/vmtest/qemu.sh install-driven, then drive with guest-opencode.sh). NOT for real hardware. The install only provides the program (the `opencode` pacman package) and the tools the guest script needs; the mcp_servers/ai_skills blocks are added by the guest script so it can start from zero the way a day-2 machine does. Needs NETWORK in the guest: `opencode plugin add` downloads from npm.",
